    "A2_RC": [
      "Operational meanings of cumulative port positions are Hausdorff and Cauchy-complete for the response-derived Gram seminorm; zero-distance positions are identified.",
      "The primitive translation readback and support seed readback factor through that same universal completion, so their labeled generator maps are the unique equal-Gram isometry rather than two independently scaled copies.",
      "Completed future-repair distinguishability is the centered equal-port response kernel, and its scale-normalized asymptotic ray defines the Gram topology on that same cumulative port-record position. The normalized infinite-response limit is taken before quotient and completion."
    ],
